secubox-portal (2.2.4-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=high

  * SECURITY: this module is a second authentication stack pointing at the
    same /etc/secubox/users.json as secubox-auth, in an incompatible shape.
    Every write rewrote the v2 store flat and downgraded argon2 hashes to
    UNSALTED SHA-256. _save_users() now refuses with 501 — user management
    belongs to secubox-auth / secubox-users.
  * SECURITY: no longer provisions a default admin/secubox account when
    users.json is missing. (ref #942)

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Fri, 31 Jul 2026 19:30:00 +0200

secubox-portal (2.2.3-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * login.html: full TOTP flow in the browser so the admin-2FA "ON" state is
    usable without the API. Login now branches on the auth response:
    - mfa_required  → 6-digit code step (POST /login/mfa; backup codes accepted)
    - enrollment_required → QR + manual-entry key + confirm step
      (POST /totp/enroll then /totp/confirm), then one-time backup codes
    - access_token  → straight in (unchanged)
    setup_required surfaces a clear message instead of a dead "Login failed".
    Verified live end-to-end on gk2 (enroll→confirm→re-login→mfa).

